{
  "scope": "Offline diagnostic. Continuous 56x32-tone burst, CP16, no gaps, fixed native (128,64), short sequential mapping. Same PA, SNR, waveforms, data, noise, CP sync, neural weights, feedback, and list decoder. Twelve pre-existing development seeds from the bounded-tracking study and historical seed 42, all included, two Dopplers paired per seed.",
  "bound": "Condition on taps and pilots; full linear map from all post-PA/pre-CP samples to all received samples (including CP, intersymbol tails and ICI), with the exact complex noise variance. E||postPA||^2 <= 56*32*f(1), f(p)=p/sqrt(1+(p/A^2)^2), by concavity, oversampled Parseval and in-band projection. Uniform information makes every native coded magnitude bit balanced. Optimize Gaussian mutual information across all singular modes by waterfilling, relaxing pilots, constellation and allowed input covariance. This gives an upper bound for the fixed modulation/coding ensemble, independent of the message and noise realization. A bound above 3328 bits cannot demonstrate achievability.",
  "fano": "For 52 uniform independent 64-bit words, average word error p of any decoder satisfies 3328-U <= 52*[h2(p)+64*p] by conditional entropy subadditivity, Fano and concavity. It bounds expected word error given this trajectory. It does not bound the realized error count.",
  "oracle": "Offline copy only. Exact complex taps and Dopplers replace the pilot fit and three feedback channel refits. The neural initializer, demapping approximation, three decoder exchanges, and list decoder remain identical. No payload truth enters either prediction path. Residual oracle errors include noise, finite code/decoder limitations and demapper mismatch; they are not a fundamental irreducible error floor. The paired BLER change is specific to this estimator.",
  "source_sha256": "2f785909b37a59b735d6c8abe77ebed2b6a6588071af0a7923ff102697d6bcb6",
  "blind_archive_cells_reproduced": 26,
